{
  "_comment": [
    "Presentation data for the 'Supported radios' table on the site.",
    "",
    "This file does NOT decide which radios appear. The row set is authoritative",
    "from radios/*/capabilities.json -- tools/gen_radio_table.py fails if this file",
    "and that directory disagree, so adding a radio cannot silently skip the site.",
    "",
    "Columns generated from capabilities.json (never listed here):",
    "  Radio name  <- capabilities.name",
    "  Modes       <- capabilities.modes  (DMR, FM, then 'AM RX' -- AM is RX-only)",
    "  Headless write backend <- capabilities.chirp -> chirp-writer,",
    "                            capabilities.benlink -> benlink.",
    "",
    "What lives here is what capabilities.json deliberately does not model: the",
    "vendor blurb, the 'hw' (verified on a physical radio) badges, whether a given",
    "third-party tool will usefully import our artifacts, and the two headless",
    "backends that are not described by a capabilities block (dmrconf, p64tool).",
    "",
    "Cell format: true | false | {\"supported\": bool, \"note\": str, \"hw\": bool}."
  ],

